# Build output. Everything under target/ regenerates from source...
target/*

# ...EXCEPT the shipped JAR, which this repo tracks on purpose. The remote has
# a commit called "fix(gui): unlock chat input + track the shipped JAR" and
# another called "build(jar): rebuild MoeGUI-1.0.0.jar from 09d8d1e", so the
# deliverable is versioned alongside the source deliberately.
#
# An earlier version of this file ignored it. That would have been a change of
# policy smuggled in as a cleanup: the JAR is what supervisor.py launches and
# what release_binaries.ps1 ships, and a repo that has the source but not the
# artifact cannot answer "which build is running".
!target/MoeGUI-1.0.0.jar

# run/ is the DEPLOY copy -- byte-identical to target/MoeGUI-1.0.0.jar, just
# placed where supervisor.py launches it from. Tracking both would put 58 MB in
# the repo per rebuild to store one artifact twice, and leave two copies that
# can disagree about which is current.
run/*.jar

dependency-reduced-pom.xml
*.class
